Used by:    core/protocol/src/main/kotlin/com/revel/obdgauge/protocol/VendoredSaeScaling.kt

kotlin-obd-api is NOT a runtime dependency of this project. Per DECISIONS.md D1, the
SAE J1979 mode-01 scaling constants and formulas for six standard PIDs (0105 coolant,
010B manifold absolute pressure, 010C engine speed, 010D vehicle speed, 010F intake air
temperature, 0133 barometric pressure) were transcribed from the source files listed in
the header of VendoredSaeScaling.kt, cross-checked against the public SAE J1979
definitions, and reimplemented in this repository. kotlin-obd-api's error-response
patterns (NO DATA / STOPPED / UNABLE TO CONNECT / "?" / BUS INIT / 7F negative response)
also informed the error typing in ResponseParser.kt.

One deliberate divergence from the vendored source is documented in VendoredSaeScaling.kt:
engine RPM is divided in floating point (SAE-exact quarter-rpm resolution) rather than by
kotlin-obd-api's truncating integer division.

